# AWS DevOps CI/CD Pipeline

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates an end-to-end CI/CD pipeline for
a Docker-based web application using AWS and GitHub.

## Architecture

GitHub
   ↓
CodePipeline
   ↓
Docker
   ↓
Amazon ECR
   ↓
Amazon EC2
   ↓
Web Application

## Technologies

- AWS
- CodePipeline
- Amazon ECR
- Amazon EC2
- Docker
- GitHub
- IAM
- CloudWatch
- Linux

## Project Steps

1. Created web application
2. Created Dockerfile
3. Containerized application
4. Uploaded source code to GitHub
5. Created ECR repository
6. Configured IAM roles
7. Created CodeBuild project
8. Built Docker image
9. Pushed image to ECR
10. Deployed Docker application on EC2
11.  Monitored builds using CloudWatch

## CI/CD Workflow

Developer pushes code to GitHub.

GitHub triggers CodePipeline.
Docker image.

The image is pushed to Amazon ECR.

The application is deployed and run using Docker on EC2.

## Result

Successfully implemented an automated CI/CD workflow
for a Docker-based web application using AWS.
